==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|streightly}}, {{m|enm|streightli}}, {{m|enm|streiȝtli}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|straight|ly}}.

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In a [[straight]] manner; so as to be straight or aligned; without curve or bend.
# Without deviation; [[directly]].
#* {{RQ:Scott Rob Roy|volume=I|page=92|passage={{...}} I was directing my course towards it, as '''straightly''' and as speedily as the windings of a very indifferent road would permit, {{...}}}}
# Immediately; straightaway.
#* {{RQ:Tyndale NT|Mark|3|12|folio=xlvij|passage=[W]hẽ the vnclene ſpritꝭ ſawe him&#11805; they fell doune before him&#11805; and cryed ſayinge: thou arte the ſonne of God: And he '''ſtreyghtly''' charged thẽ that they ſhulde not vtter him.|translation=[W]hen the unclean spirits saw him {{quote-gloss|{{w|Jesus}}}}, they fell down before him, and cried saying: thou art the son of [[w:God in Christianity|God]]: And he '''straightly''' charged them that they should not utter him.}}
#* {{RQ:R. F. Burton Arabian Nights|volume=I|chapter=XII|page=114|passage=After an hour or so the veil lifted and discovered beneath it fifty horsemen, ravening lions to the sight, in steel armour dight. We observed them '''straightly''', and lo! they were cutters-off of the highway, wild as wild Arabs.}}

